WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.797 --> 00:02.099 align:center line:81%
A school teacher once

00:02.165 --> 00:05.168 align:center line:81%
taught that a whale—even though large—

00:05.168 --> 00:09.540 align:center line:79%
could not swallow a human
because whales have small throats.

00:10.307 --> 00:13.744 align:center line:79%
A girl objected, “But
Jonah was swallowed by a whale.”

00:14.478 --> 00:16.914 align:center line:79%
The teacher responded,
“That’s impossible.”

00:17.514 --> 00:21.985 align:center line:79%
Still not convinced, the girl said, “Well,
when I go to heaven, I will ask him.”

00:23.554 --> 00:27.791 align:center line:79%
The teacher sneered, “What if Jonah was
a sinner and didn’t go to heaven?”

00:27.791 --> 00:30.394 align:center line:81%
The girl replied, “Then you can ask him.”

00:30.594 --> 00:33.096 align:center line:81%
[Laughter]

00:38.602 --> 00:42.205 align:center line:79%
We laugh, but we should not
miss the power

00:42.239 --> 00:46.443 align:center line:79%
Jonah’s story offers
every “humble seeker of happiness,”

00:46.476 --> 00:48.245 align:center line:81%
especially those struggling.

00:49.179 --> 00:53.450 align:center line:79%
God commanded Jonah to “go
to Nineveh” to declare repentance.

00:53.717 --> 00:56.954 align:center line:79%
But Nineveh was ancient
Israel’s brutal enemy—

00:57.321 --> 01:02.626 align:center line:79%
so Jonah promptly heads the exact
opposite direction, by boat, to Tarshish.

01:03.393 --> 01:07.798 align:center line:79%
As he sails away from his calling,
a shipwrecking storm develops.

01:08.298 --> 01:11.101 align:center line:81%
Certain his disobedience is the cause,

01:11.401 --> 01:14.104 align:center line:81%
Jonah volunteers to be thrown overboard.

01:15.072 --> 01:18.442 align:center line:79%
This calms the raging sea,
which saves his shipmates.

01:19.009 --> 01:21.812 align:center line:81%
Miraculously, Jonah escapes death

01:21.979 --> 01:24.915 align:center line:79%
when a “great fish” the Lord
“prepared” swallows him,

01:25.315 --> 01:28.118 align:center line:79%
but he languishes
in that unbelievably dark

01:28.118 --> 01:33.757 align:center line:79%
and putrid place for three days until
he's finally spit out on dry ground.

01:34.558 --> 01:36.560 align:center line:81%
He then accepts his call to Nineveh.

01:36.793 --> 01:40.631 align:center line:79%
Yet when the city repents
and is spared destruction,

01:40.697 --> 01:43.500 align:center line:81%
Jonah resents the mercy shown his enemies.

01:43.900 --> 01:49.940 align:center line:79%
God patiently teaches Jonah that He loves
and seeks to rescue all His children.

01:51.274 --> 01:53.877 align:center line:81%
Stumbling more than once in his duties,

01:54.077 --> 02:01.218 align:center line:79%
Jonah provides a vivid testimony
that that in mortality “all are fallen.”

02:02.252 --> 02:08.258 align:center line:79%
We don’t often speak of a testimony
of the Fall, but having a doctrinal

02:08.258 --> 02:14.464 align:center line:79%
understanding and spiritual witness
of why every single one of us struggle

02:14.631 --> 02:16.833 align:center line:81%
with moral, physical,

02:17.000 --> 02:22.105 align:center line:79%
and situational challenges is a great
blessing. Here on Earth,

02:22.472 --> 02:25.876 align:center line:81%
ugly weeds grow, even strong bones break,

02:26.109 --> 02:29.746 align:center line:81%
and all “come short of the glory of God.”

02:31.181 --> 02:35.719 align:center line:79%
But this mortal condition,
a result of choices made by Adam and Eve,

02:36.053 --> 02:39.156 align:center line:79%
is essential to the very
reason that we exist:

02:39.156 --> 02:40.557 align:center line:81%
“that [we] might have joy”!

02:41.458 --> 02:44.761 align:center line:79%
As our first parents learned,
only by tasting the bitterness

02:44.761 --> 02:48.398 align:center line:79%
and feeling the pain of a fallen
world could we even conceive of,

02:48.432 --> 02:51.134 align:center line:81%
let alone enjoy, true happiness.

02:52.135 --> 02:58.809 align:center line:79%
A testimony of the Fall does not excuse
sin or a lax approach in life’s duties,

02:58.809 --> 03:03.613 align:center line:79%
which always call for diligence,
virtue, and accountability.

03:04.715 --> 03:09.753 align:center line:79%
But it should temper our frustrations
when things just go wrong,

03:10.153 --> 03:14.825 align:center line:79%
or we see a moral failing
in a family member, friend, or leader.

03:15.659 --> 03:18.628 align:center line:79%
Rather than wallow
in contentious criticism

03:18.628 --> 03:21.565 align:center line:81%
or resentment that robs our faith,

03:21.631 --> 03:27.104 align:center line:79%
a testimony of the Fall should help
us be more like God as described by Jonah,

03:27.537 --> 03:33.110 align:center line:79%
that is, “merciful, slow to anger,
and of great kindness to all”—

03:33.543 --> 03:37.814 align:center line:79%
including ourselves
in our unavoidably imperfect state.

03:40.484 --> 03:43.520 align:center line:79%
Even greater than manifesting
the effects of the Fall,

03:43.520 --> 03:46.623 align:center line:81%
Jonah’s story powerfully directs us to Him

03:46.623 --> 03:48.892 align:center line:81%
who can deliver us from these effects.

03:49.426 --> 03:53.463 align:center line:79%
Jonah’s self-sacrifice to save
his shipmates is Christlike

03:53.463 --> 03:56.066 align:center line:81%
indeed. And three times

03:56.066 --> 04:00.137 align:center line:79%
when Jesus is pressed
for a miraculous sign of His divinity,

04:00.170 --> 04:04.708 align:center line:79%
He thunders that there shall no
sign be given but “the sign of Jonah,”

04:05.542 --> 04:09.746 align:center line:79%
declaring that as Jonah was “three days
and three nights in the whale’s belly;

04:09.880 --> 04:12.749 align:center line:81%
so shall the Son of Man be three days

04:12.749 --> 04:14.951 align:center line:79%
and three nights in
the heart of the earth.”

04:16.086 --> 04:21.892 align:center line:79%
As a symbol of the Savior’s sacrificial
death and glorious Resurrection,

04:22.726 --> 04:28.932 align:center line:79%
Jonah may be flawed. But this is also
what makes his personal witness

04:29.399 --> 04:35.739 align:center line:79%
and commitment to Jesus Christ offered
in the belly of the whale so poignant

04:35.739 --> 04:41.044 align:center line:79%
and inspiring. Jonah's
cry is that of a good man in crisis,

04:41.311 --> 04:43.413 align:center line:81%
one largely of his own making.

04:44.047 --> 04:48.785 align:center line:79%
For a Saint, when catastrophe is brought
on by a regrettable habit,

04:48.819 --> 04:53.190 align:center line:79%
comment, or decision,
despite so many other good intentions

04:53.190 --> 04:55.358 align:center line:81%
and earnest efforts of righteousness,

04:55.425 --> 05:00.096 align:center line:79%
it can be especially crushing
and leave one feeling forsaken.

05:00.931 --> 05:05.135 align:center line:79%
But whatever the cause or degree
of disaster we face,

05:05.268 --> 05:10.907 align:center line:79%
there is always dry ground for hope,
healing, and happiness.

05:12.108 --> 05:13.510 align:center line:81%
Listen to Jonah:

05:15.278 --> 05:17.714 align:center line:81%
“I cried by reason of mine

05:17.714 --> 05:19.449 align:center line:81%
affliction unto the Lord ...

05:19.883 --> 05:21.518 align:center line:81%
out of the belly of hell

05:21.551 --> 05:27.324 align:center line:79%
cried I .... For thou hadst cast me
into the deep, in the midst of the seas;

05:27.757 --> 05:31.094 align:center line:79%
and ... I said, I am
cast out of thy sight;

05:31.661 --> 05:36.132 align:center line:79%
yet I will look again
toward thy holy temple.

05:36.933 --> 05:40.737 align:center line:79%
The waters compassed me
about, even to the soul:

05:41.171 --> 05:43.206 align:center line:81%
the depth closed me round about,

05:43.206 --> 05:45.375 align:center line:81%
the weeds were wrapped about my head.

05:45.408 --> 05:47.911 align:center line:79%
I went down to the bottoms
of the mountains; ...

05:48.445 --> 05:52.549 align:center line:79%
yet hast thou brought up
my life from corruption ....

05:53.817 --> 05:57.520 align:center line:79%
When my soul fainted,
I remembered the Lord:

05:57.520 --> 06:00.724 align:center line:79%
and my prayer came ...
into thine holy temple.

06:02.125 --> 06:09.299 align:center line:79%
They that observe lying
vanities forsake their own mercy.

06:11.001 --> 06:15.438 align:center line:79%
But I will sacrifice unto thee
with the voice of thanksgiving;

06:15.739 --> 06:18.742 align:center line:81%
I will pay that that I have vowed.

06:19.409 --> 06:21.845 align:center line:81%
Salvation is of the Lord.”

06:25.916 --> 06:27.651 align:center line:81%
Though it was many years ago,

06:28.485 --> 06:34.157 align:center line:79%
I can tell you exactly where I was sitting
and exactly what I was thinking

06:34.724 --> 06:38.828 align:center line:79%
and feeling when, deep
in the belly of a personal hell,

06:39.429 --> 06:41.131 align:center line:81%
I discovered this scripture.

06:42.432 --> 06:47.604 align:center line:79%
For anyone today feeling like I did then—
that you are cast off,

06:48.271 --> 06:53.343 align:center line:79%
sinking in the deepest waters
with seaweed wrapped about your head

06:53.343 --> 06:56.479 align:center line:79%
and oceanic mountains
crashing all around you—

06:56.646 --> 06:59.849 align:center line:81%
my plea, inspired by Jonah, is:

06:59.883 --> 07:03.153 align:center line:81%
Forsake not your own mercy.

07:04.354 --> 07:10.961 align:center line:79%
You have immediate access to divine
help and healing despite your human flaws.

07:12.128 --> 07:19.302 align:center line:79%
This awe-inspiring mercy comes in and
through Jesus Christ. Because He knows

07:19.302 --> 07:20.904 align:center line:81%
and loves you perfectly,

07:21.037 --> 07:26.810 align:center line:79%
He offers it to you as your own,
meaning it's perfectly suited to you,

07:27.310 --> 07:33.249 align:center line:79%
designed to relieve your individual
agonies and heal your particular pains.

07:34.551 --> 07:39.923 align:center line:79%
So for heaven's sake and yours,
do not turn your back on that.

07:40.824 --> 07:47.998 align:center line:79%
Accept it. Start by refusing to listen
to the “lying vanities” of the adversary,

07:48.031 --> 07:51.568 align:center line:79%
who would tempt you into thinking
that relief is found

07:51.568 --> 07:55.405 align:center line:79%
in sailing away from
your spiritual responsibilities.

07:56.106 --> 08:00.310 align:center line:79%
Instead, follow the lead
of the repentant Jonah.

08:01.478 --> 08:05.081 align:center line:81%
Cry unto God. Turn to the temple.

08:06.049 --> 08:07.784 align:center line:81%
Cling to your covenants.

08:08.351 --> 08:14.824 align:center line:79%
Serve the Lord, His Church, and others
with sacrifice and thanksgiving.

08:16.092 --> 08:22.899 align:center line:79%
Doing these things brings a vision
of God’s special covenantal love for you,

08:23.466 --> 08:26.269 align:center line:81%
what the Hebrew Bible calls “hesed.”

08:27.370 --> 08:34.811 align:center line:79%
You will see and feel the power
of God's loyal, untiring, inexhaustible,

08:35.011 --> 08:40.784 align:center line:79%
and “tender mercies” that can make you
“mighty unto deliverance” from any sin

08:40.917 --> 08:42.385 align:center line:81%
or any setback.

08:43.787 --> 08:47.690 align:center line:79%
Early and intense anguish
may cloud that vision at first,

08:48.058 --> 08:52.395 align:center line:79%
but as you continue
to “pay that that [you] have vowed,”

08:52.829 --> 08:57.033 align:center line:79%
such a vision will shine
brighter and brighter in your soul.

08:57.901 --> 09:03.073 align:center line:79%
And with that vision,
you will not only find hope and healing,

09:03.306 --> 09:05.809 align:center line:81%
but astonishingly,

09:06.276 --> 09:10.346 align:center line:79%
you will find joy even
in the midst of your crucible.

09:11.381 --> 09:14.951 align:center line:81%
President Nelson taught us so well:

09:15.952 --> 09:21.091 align:center line:79%
“When the focus of our lives
is on God’s plan of salvation ...

09:21.558 --> 09:24.060 align:center line:81%
and Jesus Christ and His gospel,

09:24.427 --> 09:31.601 align:center line:79%
we can feel joy regardless of what is
happening—or not happening—in our lives.

09:31.868 --> 09:34.838 align:center line:81%
Joy comes from and because of Him.”

09:35.972 --> 09:41.010 align:center line:79%
Whether we are facing a deep
Jonah-like catastrophe

09:41.678 --> 09:45.115 align:center line:79%
or the everyday challenges
of our imperfect

09:45.115 --> 09:48.618 align:center line:81%
world, the invitation is the same:

09:49.018 --> 09:52.755 align:center line:81%
Forsake not your own mercy.

09:53.690 --> 09:58.161 align:center line:79%
Look to the sign of Jonah,
the living Christ,

09:58.628 --> 10:03.933 align:center line:79%
He who rose from His three-day grave,
having conquered all for you.

10:05.201 --> 10:07.904 align:center line:81%
Turn to Him. Believe in Him.

10:08.505 --> 10:15.778 align:center line:79%
Serve Him. Smile. For in Him
and in Him alone is found the full

10:15.778 --> 10:18.014 align:center line:81%
and happy healing from the Fall

10:18.214 --> 10:21.384 align:center line:81%
we all so urgently need and humbly seek.

10:21.951 --> 10:27.223 align:center line:79%
I testify this is true
in the sacred name of Jesus Christ,

10:27.423 --> 10:28.424 align:center line:81%
amen.

